WEBVTT

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:40.280
Oh, so cute!

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.620
She's just as I expected.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.840
Karin, that's enough.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.380
Seriously, you come out after a month and behave like this.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.670
A month?!

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:02.430
Karin comes here once every few years, and when she does, she stays for ages in Kougarou.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.100
She occupies the room for a long time. You could say she's a nuisance.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.190
Did you say something, Kochou?

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.150
No, nothing at all.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.990
Th-This can't be!

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.240
What's the matter?

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:25.830
Kochou, I'm going out for a while, but leave the room as it is!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.330
I wonder what's wrong.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.380
Dunno. Even I don't understand her sometimes.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:40.590
Anyway, Karin's a connoisseur. She's quite famous in her field.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:46.140
But, I wonder why she was so surprised about this forgery?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.020
Kochou-nee-san...

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.810
Did something happen?

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:57.900
Well, just now, a fool got swept away when the water was released in the Shouto River.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:00.990
Well, that is foolish.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:06.540
Yeah, and that fool was carrying a map to Shuurei-oujo-san's place.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.120
Do you know a fool that has a golden raccoon?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.920
A golden raccoon...

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.130
Um...

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.680
If he's bothering you, I can throw that fool back in the river right away.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.770
I-I might know someone like that, so please spare him.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:41.820
So this fool proposed marriage to you, Shuurei-chan?

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.030
Unless I heard him wrong, or he mistook me for someone else, he said something like that.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.750
In that case I'll be gentle... Not!

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:52.370
Ouch!

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.170
Why didn't you come? Seriously.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:04.760
Then I could've accomplished my mission and gone home.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.220
I gave you the letter.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.310
You know, at the gate, together with the scroll.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.940
A love letter?!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.280
Well okay, I did things in the wrong order by mistake.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.400
But I did everything, didn't I?

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:28.490
A love letter, a gift, and a proposal.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:31.330
Been there, done that, mission accomplished.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.370
This is the love letter, and...

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.790
don't tell me that's the gift?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.630
The raccoon is mine!

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.710
The gift is that scroll.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.420
Ah, I see...

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:49.850
I bought the raccoon the moment I saw it 'cause someone told me I'd be a ladies' man if I had it.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.320
So, you got swept away by the river while waiting for me?

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.740
I didn't think the river would surge like that.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.530
It's baloney. I should've been home by now with all my tasks finished.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.160
Anyway, who are you, and where are you from?

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:13.830
Huh?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.540
Did I maybe forget to include my name?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.460
I'm Shin Suou.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.130
You haven't mistaken me for someone else?

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.050
Did you actually come to propose to me?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.260
That's right.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.840
My dad told me to.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:34.180
If I marry you, some kind of powerful noble will give us money and a title.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.810
So, while I'm suspended, somebody wants me to resign quietly,

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.530
as though it were a normal consequence of getting married?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.490
Yeah, something like that.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.240
Don't you think you're being too honest here?

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:55.040
There are lots of people who want you to resign.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.000
What's the point of hiding it?

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.090
I'm going. I have work to do.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.800
Hey, Santa!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.390
Your Highness! Where are you hiding?!

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:19.350
A bride! You need a bride! Your Majesty?!

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.650
Um, excuse me...

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.360
This is Kougarou, correct?

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.320
Yes, it is.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:37.250
I just wanted to ask you. Is there a lady called Karin here?

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.670
No. I'm sorry, but there's no lady with that name here.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.170
I see.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.460
Thank you very much.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:56.180
You seemed full of confidence, but what if there is a woman called Karin here?

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.020
No, there isn't.

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:04.360
I carry the names and faces of all the women of Kougarou in my head.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:08.240
I see, impressive! As expected of Shuuei!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.910
Santa! What's wrong with you all of sudden?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.290
Huh, is that Shuurei-dono's voice?

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:30.970
What are you doing?!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.180
Please stop, Your Highness.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.010
Where do you think you're touching?

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.600
It's cramped in here. I can't help it!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.020
I'm not touching you because I want to!

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.900
What were you-

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:58.330
I didn't want to hear you say something like that about your own marriage.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:02.120
As if it's part of some sort of deal, as if it's nothing.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.330
As if it's someone else's business.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.710
Santa...

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.420
If you hadn't become an officer,
you wouldn't say things like that.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.130
You'd have fallen in love like everyone else,

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.050
got married like everyone else,

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.970
and lived happily like everyone else.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.730
I know... what you did in Sashuu.

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.150
Are you really okay with this?

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:30.860
What did you gain from trying so hard?!

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.360
You were robbed of everything,
and in the end you were suspended?

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:40.490
I know you realize it, but you've been used as a scapegoat!

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.790
Aren't you disappointed?!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.170
Being used by the Emperor and higher officials all the time!

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:50.880
I know that you always looked ahead and did your best.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.880
I'm always playing around, but you're really amazing.

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:56.430
But!

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:02.520
I can't see you ever being happy as a woman!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.020
Shuurei...

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.450
Hey, Shuurei, couldn't this be the place for you?

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.910
There are plenty of people who recognize and follow you.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.200
Couldn't this city be the place for you?!

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:27.750
You can find all the happiness you want here.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:32.550
You still want to work hard as an officer?!

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.550
For the ones who took away your official rank? Even now?!

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.310
Oh? A new face?

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:45.180
A new face?

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:50.770
Good timing. Can you weigh the coins I got from selling a painting recently and enter them in the books?

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.690
So, I'll leave it to you.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.450
Weigh them, huh?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.420
That shook you, didn't it, Shuurei-chan?

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:10.750
To be honest, yes.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:17.220
Santa has tried hard ever since he heard you'd become an officer.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:19.430
Tried hard?

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.850
That's right. He got serious and started to work really hard.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:31.060
He probably thought he should do
something to compete against you.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:32.900
Santa did?

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.820
Santa has become quite a man.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:45.950
That was a low blow.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:47.290
Yeah.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:55.340
It's what oujo-sama decided.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.130
Seiran...

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:03.300
Your Highness knew it all and regrets none of it,

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.350
but if Kouyuu-dono and Ran-shogun look like that,

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.520
he's left without a leg to stand on.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.030
Wh-What's that?!

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:29.870
Like I said, some bloke asked me to weigh them.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:36.670
Th-That blo- That old master said this was his payment from selling the painting, correct?

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.590
That's right.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:39.510
Kochou-nee-san...

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.930
Have you noticed what's wrong with these scales?

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:48.930
The number of coins on the plates are different, yet they balance!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.310
Th-This can't be! Counterfeit coins?!

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:56.060
How dare they challenge Kougarou like this!

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.530
Oh, they're counterfeit coins.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.400
They're well made.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.820
It's skilled work.

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:09.580
If you hadn't noticed, this could've gone undiscovered for a long time.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:11.290
Suou-san.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:12.120
What?

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.290
You're an officer, aren't you?

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.170
I've got an officer's rank.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.920
You aren't on suspension like I am, are you?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.510
I don't do things that would get me suspended.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.260
In that case, let's work on this together!

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.680
Here, right away!

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:26.390
No way.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.430
I was only told to propose to you.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.270
I'll just get my job done and leave.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:36.310
Hey kid, your family's not uninvolved either.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.150
This gift you gave to Shuurei-chan...

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:42.150
It's also a forgery!

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.570
That's so typical of my dad.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.330
He gets cheated very easily.

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.080
Then all the more reason you should come with me!

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.330
He's a victim! Your father!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:13:01.090
Yeah, but Dad hasn't realized he's a victim yet.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.340
Don't be so casual about things.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:10.970
If you aren't going with her, expect to experience hell...

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:14.060
I will go with pleasure!

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.390
As expected of Kochou-nee-san!

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.900
That must've been what's called "using one's sexual charm."

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.570
That was what's called "blackmail"!

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:27.160
Shuurei-chan, the works I judged to be forgeries are all kept at gang boss Rakan's place, so you'd better go see him.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:30.030
Together with Seiran.

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.870
Did you call me, oujo-sama?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.250
Seiran!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:51.850
Really, even when she's suspended, she finds work to do all by herself and goes shooting off...

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.330
right?

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:58.520
Ran-sama, you knew about this, didn't you?

00:13:58.980 --> 00:13:59.520
I apologize.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.730
Will you leave Shuurei-chan on her own?

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:04.730
Seiran's with her. She'll be all right.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:07.900
More importantly, there's something I want to ask you.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.410
I heard that Heki Yuukoku is in the district.

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.500
Do you have any information?

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:17.290
That Yuukoku is?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:22.460
Let me see. I might know someone who could have a clue.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:23.960
Really?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.260
Karin, who's staying here a while, might...

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:28.300
Karin?

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:29.970
Back then...

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.220
I was wrong.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:36.270
So, who is this person named Karin?

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.020
She's a connoisseur.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:43.480
If anyone knows about Yuukoku, she does.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.360
Is that lady here now?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:50.280
Well, the thing is... She dashed out like a bullet.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:53.660
I'd think it'd be faster if you went to look for her...

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:59.290
but she's a little harsh on men, so be careful.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.750
You spoil that snotty brat too much!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.590
There's no need for you to undertake everything and become his shield!

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.010
Resign as Prime Minister, or you'll die.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.770
Maybe, but there's something I want.

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.560
Something you... want?

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.480
What is it? I'll give you as much as you like.

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:28.030
No, it's something I can only get by risking my life.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:32.950
I find it unpleasant to watch you kneel to that snotty brat!

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:34.910
Resign as Prime Minister right now!

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:37.040
Forget about that brat!

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.120
Choose me!

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:44.170
No, Reishin. Choose me, please.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:47.920
Even though you've become the Prime Minister, I won't change.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:52.260
I don't care about this country, and I dislike the royal family.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.010
I don't want you to change.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:58.560
So I'll leave it to your free will.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:03.100
Anyway, it will be all right for the time being.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.230
Rin made me a camouflaged weapon for protecting myself.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:08.980
A camouflaged weapon?

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:14.410
Yes. If I recall correctly, I turn the stick's handle like this, and...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:19.870
Oh?

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:21.040
What do you mean, "Oh"?!

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.000
Do you intend to become a street performer?!

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.880
What's this? Pepper?

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:34.840
To even fool Reishin... as expected of my great wife.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:42.600
You can stay in this room and help me work until you regain your dignity as the "Minister of Ice," if you want.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.150
It's best to run!

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:52.490
I can't bear to be involved anymore.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.280
A bamboo shoot?

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.120
Is that guy a devil?

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:09.840
Tan-tan-kun...

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.340
Tan-tan?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.010
Tan-tan-kun of the Tan-tan-tanuki.

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:22.220
If you're a man, don't you think you should keep your word?

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.350
No, not really.

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:28.060
Hey, you two! Don't go ahead without me!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.310
Oh? Bamboo shoots?

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:31.440
How come?

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.610
How about these for dinner?

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.530
A good idea!

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.610
It's the height of the season for them too!

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.070
Yes.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:46.910
The woman named Karin seems to be visiting each and every shop that sells paintings.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.920
The painting and calligraphic art stores.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.170
Those stores?

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:57.590
When she finds a forgery, she points it out and goes dashing off to the next store.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:01.100
Get out of my way, you bastards over there!

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.850
You're in my way!

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:11.360
What was that boar-like creature?!

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.690
That was rude, Kouyuu.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:15.530
She was quite good looking.

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:18.570
I was called a bastard for the first time...

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.990
Oh? Hey, hottie! Where ya goin'?

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.750
Get lost!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.880
Honestly, men!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:33.840
They're synonymous with vermin! Die and redo your life!

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:44.100
Oh, that's impressive. Shuurei-dono can even go into gang boss Rakan's place?

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.390
Who's gang boss Rakan?

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.060
He ranks above Kochou. He's the boss of the bosses.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:54.360
She's taken the forgeries that were stored at Rakan's.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:19:00.110
Also, she asked him to inform her if there are any complaints about housewares.

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.740
Shuurei's working on the same problem as the Ministry of Justice.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:05.410
Isn't the matter getting serious?

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.160
Well, Shuurei doesn't know the
Ministry of Justice is taking action.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.000
True...

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.210
Normally, what she's doing would be right...

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:17.800
but the current Minister of Justice gets what he wants by fair means or foul.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.380
On top of that, I hear he has a high opinion of himself.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:24.350
Yes... If the Ministry of Justice finds out about her, they won't be impressed.

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:30.560
For now, we have to find Karin quickly and learn the whereabouts of Yuukoku-dono!

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.940
Apparently Karin's quite a beauty.

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:36.070
I'm looking forward to meeting her.

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:39.780
What if she's like that boar just now?

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:45.120
No way, a woman with such a gentle-sounding name as "Karin" couldn't possibly be...

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:50.960
Ah, it's true the woman just now was also a beauty, but...

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.210
It can't be.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.750
No, it can't...

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:04.050
Your Highness! Take a bride! Your Highness!!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:11.430
Why does so much work pile up when Kouyuu-sama isn't here?!

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:14.100
Really, this is serious, it's bad, it's not good at all.

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:17.570
If Yuukoku is here, that means the other two are as well!

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:22.280
They could be visiting the mansion right now.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:25.870
Argh, I can't finish the work!

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.870
Because of his work, Hakumei-kun is not here.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:34.170
But, seriously, where has she gone?

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:40.170
Oh well, Karin-san is probably with that child.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.850
It's a bit odd.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.770
In order to convince customers that the forgeries are the originals,

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:57.060
there's a condition that has to be fulfilled, isn't there?

00:20:57.560 --> 00:20:58.520
A condition?

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:01.400
That's right. They mustn't be found.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.690
Oh, the originals?

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:10.160
If the whereabouts of the originals were known,
any attempt to sell a fake would be discovered quickly.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:13.040
So the whereabouts of the originals has to remain unknown.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:20.130
In that case, the mysterious art dealer
who's selling the fakes has the originals.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:24.420
Indeed. Tan-tan, you're smart.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:28.930
The mysterious art dealer buys the original artworks from the rich and the nobility,

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.640
creates forgeries of them,

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:32.720
and sells them as the originals.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:39.900
In addition, if you pay for the originals with counterfeit coins, you earn twice as much.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:42.530
What's wrong, Tan-tan-kun?

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.940
You're suddenly quick on the uptake.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:48.360
Nothing...

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:52.740
Take a look at this forgery for a second.

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:58.500
This... It's similar to Yuukoku's work somehow.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:02.750
You think so? Me too.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:08.430
It's similar, but I can't say it's definitely by Yuukoku.

00:22:09.010 --> 00:22:11.430
I can't say that with confidence either.

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:18.770
However, I'm certain the creator of this forgery has something to do with Yuukoku.

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:22.820
Perhaps he's related to the Heki family.

00:22:23.360 --> 00:22:28.990
If so, it's likely that the creator is being forced to make forgeries.

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:30.070
True.

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:38.960
Your Highness, I understand your feelings, but we must start heading back.

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:43.670
Yes, though I'd have preferred to ascertain Yuukoku-dono's whereabouts today.

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:47.210
There's plenty of other work to do as well.

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:48.590
I know that.

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:51.890
We'll search for him again tomorrow afternoon.

00:22:53.550 --> 00:22:56.140
Get out of the way over there!

00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:59.140
Now then, we'll go to the next place!

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:08.860
Seiran?

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.910
What's wrong? We're going.

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:14.620
I'm coming, oujo-sama.

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:19.790
Someone's been following us all this time.

00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:46.790
Fake paintings are circulating in the market.

00:24:47.170 --> 00:24:49.920
Little by little, pots, pans, and salt are getting more expensive.

00:24:50.340 --> 00:24:51.960
There's someone behind this.

00:24:51.960 --> 00:24:53.970
It smells fishy.

00:24:53.970 --> 00:24:56.800
Huh? There's a nice smell of bamboo shoots too.
